" class=3D"pt-5 m-auto lightense-target" role=3D"presentation" referrerpoli=
cy=3D"no-referrer" src=3D"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:700/1*BpeNA=
sOj-3V575b2ZC_cqQ@2x.png"></div><p class=3D"leading-8 mt-7">The cumulative =
distribution function (CDF) of a random variable <em>X</em> is the function=
 given by:</p><div class=3D"mt-7"><img loading=3D"eager" alt=3D"None" class=
=3D"pt-5 m-auto lightense-target" role=3D"presentation" referrerpolicy=3D"n=
o-referrer" src=3D"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:700/1*p2LHYKucnyF4=
OIoV_kwNYA@2x.png"></div><p class=3D"leading-8 mt-7">For a discrete random =
variable, this is equal to the sum of the probabilities of all the outcomes=
 in which the value of <em>X</em> is less than or equal to <em>x</em>. Math=
ematically:</p><div class=3D"mt-7"><img loading=3D"eager" alt=3D"None" clas=
s=3D"pt-5 m-auto lightense-target" role=3D"presentation" referrerpolicy=3D"=
no-referrer" src=3D"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:700/1*5aZPK1V3utq=
s269rAJRBqw@2x.png"></div><p class=3D"leading-8 mt-7">The <em>mean</em> or =
<em>expectation</em> of a discrete random variable <em>X</em>, denoted by <=
em>E</em>(<em>X</em>), is a number defined as follows:</p><div class=3D"mt-=
7"><img loading=3D"eager" alt=3D"None" class=3D"pt-5 m-auto lightense-targe=
